        "original_id": "e23be1f2-7f85-59c7-a96a-b2c771e4390c",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Street Survivors, That Smell\n- People: Steve Gaines, Ronnie Van Zant, Allen Collins, Cassie Gaines\n- Organizations: Lynyrd Skynyrd\n- Topics: Southern rock\n\nFacts:\n- Street Survivors is the fifth studio album by Southern rock band Lynyrd Skynyrd, and it was released on October 17, 1977.\n- Street Survivors was the last Lynyrd Skynyrd album recorded by original members Ronnie Van Zant and Allen Collins.\n- Street Survivors is the only Lynyrd Skynyrd studio recording to feature guitarist Steve Gaines.\n- Steve Gaines, born Steven Earl Gaines on September 14, 1949, was an American musician.\n- Steve Gaines was a guitarist, vocalist, and songwriter for Lynyrd Skynyrd from May 11, 1976 until his death on October 20, 1977.\n- Cassie Gaines was Steve Gaines's older sister and sang backup vocals during Lynyrd Skynyrd live performances.\n- That Smell was written by Ronnie Van Zant and Allen Collins.\n- That Smell was released in 1977 on the album Street Survivors.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
